      "sender": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::ClaudeAcpPersona",
      "id": "04308495-9861-4be4-a0d6-4e697196fde4",
      "body": "Two different concerns here \u2014 your own notebook, and something already off in the shared template. Quick flag first: `git status` shows you've locally modified `downstream_apps/template/configs/config_script.yaml` (setting `s3_cache_dir` to your home path) \u2014 that's the **shared template**, not your `flare_forecast` copy. That's exactly the kind of edit you were warned about; it's currently uncommitted, so just don't stage/commit it (or revert with `git checkout -- ../template/configs/config_script.yaml`).\n\nYour `flare_forecast` app is already its own fork (own `FlareDSDataset`, `FlareMetrics`, own config), so the dataset/model/metrics code is not something you need to fork further \u2014 it's the shared code for this specific task. What's actually machine/person-specific in **`1_baseline_template.ipynb`**:\n\n1. **`os.environ[\"CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES\"]`** (cell `6d6af87a`) \u2014 currently `\"0\"`. Set this to whatever GPU your team/machine was actually assigned, per the markdown warning right above it.\n2. **`run_name`** in the WandB cell (`48c4d138`) \u2014 currently `\"baseline_experiment_1_\"`. Give each run you launch a distinct, descriptive name so it doesn't collide with teammates' runs in the same `wandb_project`.\n3. **`wandb_entity`** in `configs/config_script.yaml` under `logging:` \u2014 `null` logs to your personal account; set it only if you're meant to log into a shared team entity/project.\n4. **`s3_cache_dir`** in `configs/config_script.yaml` (`data:` section) \u2014 it's currently committed as `/home/jovyan/scratch_space/surya_cache`. If that path is common to everyone's container that's fine, but ADAPTING.md's stated preference is to *not* bake this into the committed YAML \u2014 use `--s3-cache-dir` on the CLI or `export SURYA_WS_CACHE_DIR=...` per-machine instead, so the committed file stays generic.\n5. If you start checkpointing (later notebooks), watch `output.ckpt_dir` / `output.s3_prefix` \u2014 give yourself a unique prefix so you don't overwrite a teammate's `best.ckpt`.\n\nNothing else in this notebook needs personalizing \u2014 it already imports everything generic from `workshop_infrastructure/` and everything flare-specific from your own `flare_forecast/` modules.",
      "raw_time": false
    },
