      "mentions": [],
      "raw_time": false,
      "body": "That's the `save_dir` arg in the `WandbLogger` cell (`48c4d138`):\n\n```python\nwandb_logger = WandbLogger(\n    ...\n    save_dir=\"./wandb/wandb_tmp\",\n)\n```\n\nIt's a relative path, resolved against the notebook kernel's working directory \u2014 which for a Jupyter notebook is the directory the `.ipynb` file lives in, i.e. `/home/jovyan/tmp/surya_workshop/downstream_apps/flare_forecast`. So once you run that cell, it'll create `flare_forecast/wandb/wandb_tmp/` (it doesn't exist yet \u2014 you haven't run this notebook in this session).\n\nThis is local scratch storage for wandb's run cache before/while it syncs to the cloud \u2014 it's not shared with teammates just because the repo is shared (it lives under your own `/home/jovyan`, not in git). So the default is already fine to use as-is; you don't need to personalize it unless you want it outside the repo tree (e.g. to keep it off anything that might get committed, or to point it at your scratch space instead of home):\n\n```python\nsave_dir=\"/home/jovyan/scratch_space/wandb\",\n```\n\nSeparately, this is *not* the same as which WandB account/project the run is logged to \u2014 that's `wandb_entity`/`wandb_project` in `configs/config_script.yaml`, which we covered earlier.",
